            0.457
          ],
          "content": "■ Becoming a better programmer"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.468,
            0.846,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "\\- Exposure to a few extra features of Python and some useful libraries"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.577,
            0.488,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": "\\- Practice, practice, practice"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.968,
            0.55,
            0.986
          ],
          "content": "6.0002 LECTURE 15"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.892,
            0.968,
            0.911,
            0.989
          ],
          "content": "18"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 15,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.035,
            0.542,
            0.098
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Optimization Problems"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.174,
            0.781,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": "■Many problems can be formulated in terms of"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.235,
            0.383,
            0.28
          ],
          "content": "\\- Objective function"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.294,
            0.368,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": "\\- Set of constraints"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.37,
            0.563,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "■ Greedy algorithms often useful"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.431,
            0.587,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": "\\- But may not find optimal solution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.507,
            0.866,
            0.558
          ],
          "content": "■ Many optimization problems inherently exponential"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.568,
            0.661,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": "\\- But dynamic programming often works"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.627,
            0.76,
            0.674
          ],
          "content": "\\- And memoization a generally useful technique"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.704,
            0.889,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": "■Examples: knapsack problems, graph problems, curve fitting, clustering"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.967,
            0.55,
            0.987
          ],
          "content": "6.0002 LECTURE 15"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.893,
            0.965,
            0.911,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "19"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.034,
            0.471,
            0.099
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Stochastic Thinking"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.173,
            0.749,
            0.225
          ],
          "content": "■The world is (predictably) non-deterministic"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.251,
            0.803,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": "■Thinking in terms of probabilities is often useful"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.329,
            0.735,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "■Randomness is a powerful tool for building computations that model the world"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.461,
            0.901,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": "■ Random computations useful even when for problems that do not involve randomness"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.573,
            0.346,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": "\\- E.g., integration"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.968,
            0.55,
            0.986
          ],
          "content": "6.0002 LECTURE 15"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.892,
            0.969,
            0.911,
            0.989
          ],
          "content": "20"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 17,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.033,
            0.489,
            0.099
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Modeling the World"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.167,
            0.454,
            0.209
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "■Models always inaccurate"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.211,
            0.503,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": "\\- Provide abstractions of reality"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.275,
            0.733,
            0.323
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "■ Deterministic models, e.g., graph theoretic"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.341,
            0.363,
            0.385
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "■Statistical models"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.389,
            0.717,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": "\\- Simulation models: Monte Carlo simulation"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.439,
            0.495,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": "\\- Models based on sampling"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.486,
            0.524,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": "\\- Characterizing accuracy is critical"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.529,
            0.404,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": "\\- Central limit theorem"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.569,
            0.321,
            0.605
          ],
          "content": "\\- Empirical rule"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.609,
            0.39,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": "\\- Machine learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.658,
            0.488,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": "\\- Unsupervised and supervised"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.719,
            0.38,
            0.759
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "■ Presentation of data"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.764,
            0.231,
            0.805
          ],
          "content": "\\- Plotting"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.808,
            0.425,
            0.849
          ],
          "content": "\\- Good and bad practices"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.968,
            0.55,
            0.986
          ],
          "content": "6.0002 LECTURE 15"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.892,
            0.969,
            0.911,
            0.989
          ],
          "content": "21"
        }
      ]
